# Workers Static Assets serves the deploy directory verbatim, and this project
# deploys from the repo root. Without this file the whole .git directory ships
# as public static assets - /.git/config and /.git/objects/* returned HTTP 200
# on the first deploy, which lets anyone reconstruct the full repository.
#
# Do not remove. Anything listed here is excluded from the upload.
.git/**
.wrangler/**
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.assetsignore
wrangler.jsonc

# Worker source. It is bundled into the Worker at build time and does not need
# to be reachable over HTTP as well. Serving it published the honeypot field
# name, the time-to-fill threshold and the exact rate-limit values, which is
# everything a bot author needs to walk straight past all three.
worker/**
